 HISTORY                                                            27 1451
 -------                                                            27 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    27 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The          27 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section libraries for Be in BeO were    27 1451
 fully developed using ab-initio lattice dynamics (AILD) methods    27 1451
 [1]. BeO has a hexagonal wurtzite crystal structure with           27 1451
 symmetry belonging to the P6_3mc space group (#186). It was        27 1451
 modeled in VASP [2-4] using the GGA-PBE exchange-correlation       27 1451
 functional with a 450 eV plane wave energy cutoff and a 6x6x3      27 1451
 Monkhorst-Pack k-space mesh. The DOS was calculated in PHONON      27 1451
 [5] via the dynamical matrix method using a 4x4x2 supercell.       27 1451
 Eight temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law     27 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to produce MT     27 1451
 = 2 (coherent) and MT = 4 data [6]. By convention, MAT=27 and      27 1451
 ZA=127 are used for Be in BeO. This evaluation improves upon       27 1451
 the Be_BeO evaluation in ENDF/B-VIII.0 by (1) updating the mass    27 1451
 and free atom cross section of O to be those of the                27 1451
 naturally-weighted element and (2) using experimental lattice      27 1451
 parameters in the calculation of the coherent elastic (MT=2)       27 1451
 data [7-8]. The impact of both changes is restricted to MT=2 of    27 1451
 this evaluation for Be in BeO. The atomic masses and free atom     27 1451
 cross sections were taken from the ENDF/B-VIII.0 database [9],     27 1451
 with the latter corresponding to 1.0E-05 eV. The natural           27 1451
 abundances of the O isotopes were taken from the NIST database     27 1451
 [10].                                                              27 1451
